{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae","id":1384313,"title":"Garou Packs of Stag among the Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-27T17:59:46-07:00","id":1384313,"title":"Garou Packs of Stag among the Fae","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I am doing research to help me figure out some ways to include a Garou pack with the Stag totem in the world of the Fae. This is for a Werewolf game, but I wanted to get insight from players of Changeling.This is specifically about Garou packs with the Stag totem, which is something I have not found specifically mentioned in Changeling books. The only Garou references I find are vague generalities concerning tribes. But packs of Stag have a concrete ban involving aiding the Fae so it is something that should be explored in more detail.<br /> <br /> So after looking at existing material</span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> talking about Garou/Fae interaction, particularly in regards to the Fianna (for obvious reasons, although the tribe does not have a Ban unlike packs), and also research into the role of actual Irish warbands (real world historical and mythological fianna) as an inspiration</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">, I've come up with some ideas and wanted to run it by you. My goals are to get an idea of what elements of Changeling should be included if I want to run a good integration between the game lines; find a balance between making the ban real as restriction on the PCs, but keeping player autonomy; allowing the ST (me) to use this as an RP tool, but not trapping me to run a Fae dominant game.<br /> <br /> Looking for feedback here on how well you think this could be incorporated from a Changeling specific. In other words, rather than how to fit Changelings into Werewolf, I am wondering how a Changeling game would handle a Garou pack of Stag as a normal part of their setting. While not all domains of Changeling would have a local pack of Stag to call upon, it should be common enough that a sizable minority would have access to one. I can then work back as needed to determine how it appears from a Garou perspective for a Werewolf game.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If there are parts people disagree with, or believe new parts should be added for consideration, let's hear them and the reasons why.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:03:07-07:00","id":1384315,"title":"","content":"Here's some general principles on the nature of the connection between these packs on the Fae. I've used them to determine some general principles, so changes here will affect things downstream.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">On the Nature of Stag (and his Children) and the Fae</span></span></b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Stag Incarna spirit has a special role among the Fae. Perhaps because of some pact between Stag and the Tuatha de Danaan. Perhaps some other reason.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">While some interaction with the Fae will be done in the real world, at some points these packs should also be entering freeholds and the Near Dreaming.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Ban of Stag represents something very real between those Garou and the Fae. There is an implied Oath between that pack and the Fae. That \u201cOath\u201d should drive the relationship between these two groups. It'd be nice to have an articulated one, but simply having guidelines to give to PCs should be enough.</span></span></li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-27-2020, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:06:15-07:00","id":1384316,"title":"","content":"Now I had to ask myself what are the general rules that govern relations between actual Garou and the local fae based on the totem ban. So this would set expectations for both kinds of PCs (Garou and Changelings). I wanted expectations to be clear, but flexible. And open to many kinds of specific details between chronicles.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">On the role of Packs of Stag among the Fae</span></span></b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Packs of Stag are semi-independent band of hunter-warriors pledged to protect the Dreaming. Children of Stag, in exchange for their Totem's patronage, are expected to keep order and protect the Fae on Stag's behalf.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">While packs of Stag have the duty to aid the fey, there are limits to what the fey can ask of them. No fae can command the pack (although as relationships develop, individual packs and members of such packs might decide to swear additional oaths on their own in exchange for other favors just like changeling can decide to swear oaths to each other). But \u201clocal\u201d fae can request help. But how to do so is left to the pack's discretion most of the time.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The primary duty of such packs is to patrol the \u201cfrontier\u201d or other dangerous territories to defend the fae from external threats (most likely malicious chimera or other invading forces), not internal policing.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Packs of stag are not obligated to involve themselves in internal fae politics, so rival fae domains at war and such don't interest them. They are more like the Night Watch in Game of Thrones \u2013 the shield that guards the realms of fae.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So there is an expectation that packs of Stag are proactive in this kind of patrol. Which means they need to be able to enter the Near Dreaming, or perhaps identify freeholds in the mundane world. This kind of knowledge can be imparted to them by their pack totem, who as a jaggling avatar should be able to follow airts, identify Trods (Garou definition, which I believe maps to the Changeling concept of the Green Paths of Balor), and have basic knowledge to serve as an interpreter and guide to the Fae to its pack.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In addition to that, packs of Stag serve as a form of mobile military reserves for the local fae. They can be called out by the local fae authority (either a fae lord, or another authority if it is a commoner held area) if there is a very big threat.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Therefore, the fae need a means to \u201csummon\u201d local packs of Stag that could help them. This could be done by various means \u2013 certain fae Treasures, certain cantrips, or personal visits. Before such summons are done, it is probably best that the Fae and Garou meet and interact so there are no surprises on either side.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Packs can also be asked to avenge wrongs done to the Fae after the fact, provided they are things the pack would have defended the Fae if they were at the right place and time to prevent.</span></span></li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-27-2020, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:09:33-07:00","id":1384317,"title":"","content":"Lastly, I needed some details on actual interaction between them, especially in terms of how these characters are introduced to one another. I have some general notions, but it is here where I'd need more specific details from forum members on how this can work.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">How the Fae and Packs of Stag Actually Meet and Interact with One Another</span></span></b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So at some point early on the pack's career, the Fae need to make contact so the Garou pack can actually fulfill its voew/ban. While some proactivity by the Garou is appreciated, since the Fae are experts on the Dreaming, they are more likely the ones to reach out first. Therefore, they have to know when a new pack of Stag is formed, or when it arrives. Again, this is probably done by appropriate Cantrips (like Soothsay) or Treasures. If you can think of other means, let me know.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Fae also need to be able to contact and request help on occasion, though contacting the Pack is not like a 911 call. Instead, it is more like a plea or petition. While a pack of Stag is obligated to assist per their ban, they may also demand \u201cpayment\u201d of some kind, or everyone understands a future favor is owed, or at least that the fae requesting help is under social obligation to the Garou pack. Every request of help further binds the Garou pack and those Fae, creating stronger bonds. But I need to figure out how a random individual Fae can do that. How can a Fae track down the pack when needed? What if it is a Fae who has never before encountered the pack? How do Fae in general learn about the pack?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Since these packs are semi-independent, almost mercenary, it is alright for packs to move around to different territories. So if they particularly don't like the fae in a certain area, or have more affinity elsewhere, it is perfectly acceptable for packs to move around so they are far enough away to not help certain fae, but can help other fae. Packs of Stag have a responsibility, but they have a lot of discretion on how to perform it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Nevertheless, as the pack increases their prowess and fame, they may see themselves getting requests from fae further away because they know of that pack's reputation and have a serious problem.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The rule of chiminage still applies. While packs of Stag aren't \u201cpaid\u201d for the protection they provide, all relationships need to be maintained by the exchange of gifts and services. While some of this is provided by the benefits of the Stag totem, the Fae should be providing the pack something to show their appreciation.</span></span></li> </ol><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I think the \u201cproper feel\u201d of a Garou pack of Stag among the Fae should be the Garou are like a marauding band of \u201cmercenaries\u201d. Hired by Stag that is. They are part of Fae society because of Stag's Oath, but not a reputable part of it. They are uncouth and dangerous. They are there to help maintain order, but could potentially pillage and raid the very people they are supposed to protect. But they might become true and valued friends of the local Fae.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If you disagree and think the relationship would be different, I am interested in hearing what you think it should be. As well as any other comments on how this relationship and oath should be depicted.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T19:08:38-07:00","id":1384337,"title":"","content":"Personally I was peeved that was never really fleshed out. I mean we get some stuff about Fianna and Fiona being allies, but say Dark Age Werewolf/Fae it didn't make any sort of sense how the Fianna had a fey history when the Dark Age Fae book was all LOL we tricked some werewolves into helping one of our gang fights what rubes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T20:13:38-07:00","id":1384345,"title":"","content":"I didn't know anything about this stag pack, pretty interesting, where can I read more?<br /> <br /> The info I can share that maybe will help is:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1- Fae probably know more about the garou than the garou do about the fae. Changelings can live pretty long lives, and sometimes they remember very well their past lives, which is also useful for remembering encounters with the garou. This might make it so the changeling knows more about the rules of a stag pack than the garous. Some of the more cunning fae might try to trick garous, using rules or pacts that never existed.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2- From the fae only nunnehi (native american changelings) can enter the umbra, at least usually. However lost trods or places in the deep dreaming or umbra might have passages to each place.<br /> <br /> 3- The stag can be either a chimera that went to umbra and become a powrful totem, or a spirit that went to the dreaming. Either way I don't think it changes it's role.<br /> <br /> 4- There are much more connection with werewolfs than simply the fianna. Read the kinfolk book for more info. Lord Li-tili of house balor is protected by black spiral dancers for example.<br /> <br /> 5- There is the shadow/nightmare court, fae who want to bring about the long winter, the death of the dreaming. They belive this will make room for a new dreaming to be born. They probably smell like wyrm, maybe old school wyrm, before it was corrupted.<br /> <br /> edit: Oh, looks like this stag stuff is from dark ages, so this might not apply since dark ages fae is very different from changeling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 04-27-2020, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T21:01:47-07:00","id":1384348,"title":"","content":"Assuming a modern CtD context, I definitely think it's fair to say that many fae have very old oaths with beings like Stag and the Fianna although like much of early Changeling history and the Dreaming, specifics can be maddeningly vague.<br /> <br /> I think one thing that can be useful is considering which fae have ties to Stag. This is largely those tied to celtic/gaelic Europe which represents most standard kiths, alongside certain kiths especially such as Sidhe of House Fiona who have the most blatant and obvious ties to the Fianna.<br /> <br /> \u2022On the Nature...<br /> -I would agree that considering the Stag incarna to be oathbound to the fae since ancient days makes sense. I can see numerous reasons for it, but what strikes me most is Stag desiring an alliance with the fae of the Dreaming (as opposed to Nightmare) in order to combat the Fomorians and protect Stag's family, whom fae too are bound with. <br /> -I would say that it's important to keep in mind that for a group of werewolves to fully involve themselves with the Fae, they will most likely need to be enchanted at some point, making calling upon them an expense of Changeling glamour reserves.<br /> <br /> \u2022Role of Stag Packs<br /> -I'd say that most of that is on the money, adding that garou are probably best served in aiding the fae as shock troops against monstrous chimera or contacts in assuring that the 'Right of Rescue' (every changelings right to be rescued and brought safely to the dreaming) is maintained.<br /> -Changelings by their nature are probably quite likely to try and draw the packs into their society, which is a whirlwind most of the time.<br /> <br /> \u2022Meeting one another<br /> -Changeling seers and scribes are a strong way for the changelings to discover packs. This might be alongside generational contacts between the changelings and the Fianna, as well as that many changeling hotspots are likely to shine like beacons to garou with the Sense Wyld gift.<br /> -I'd say as to god fae contact the pack that it's likely that a pack that wants to work with the fae would either seek their society and feedholds out or be discovered either by soothsay or chance (Changelings know that The Dreaming often puts its finger on the scale for the sake of narrative). Once contact is established, changelings might use human methods or maintain messengers and chimera and the like to reach out. As far as exchange for service, I'm sure that most changelings would happily extend the rights of the Echeat to a proven Pack of Stag.<br /> -I imagine that many packs would have little trouble building up regional networks of Changeling contacts and that changelings themselves would have little trouble spreading word. I also don't see an issue with packs relocating, although Stag may take issue if they abandon the local court in a time of emergency.<br /> -Probably yes, at which point the pack is most likely drawn into the world of Changeling politics, to some degree or another<br /> -I'd say that with most Seelie Changelings, recompense is almost guaranteed without effort. The Seelie will go out of their own way to repay the debt. Unseelie Changelings might abuse Stag's generosity, but if the situation is dire enough, packs might still be expected to intervene. Changelings are bound to their natures and the loss of even the most treacherous among them draws the Apocalypse one step closer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T10:54:40-07:00","id":1384444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384345#post1384345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't know anything about this stag pack, pretty interesting, where can I read more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stag as a pack totem is found in every Werewolf corebook going back to first edition. It's a basic part of the game. One of that totem's bans is a requirement to help fae in need. But that's about all there is. There isn't much more description, or other details on how such packs should be run (but that is the case for all pack totems, there's only a few paragraphs description). If you don't have the Werewolf corebook, you can probably find the totem write up somewhere on the internet. There's lot of ongoing or former online games that reference them. <br /> <br /> The Fianna tribebook, which deals with a tribe of Garou with Stag as the tribal totem, has more detail on culture and some Fae interactions. That can be used as partial inspiration, but packs and tribes of the same totem aren't identical. The Fianna tribe versus a a pack of Stag comprising Uktena, Wendigo, and Red Talons, or a pack of Stag with a Get of Fenris, Shadow Lord, and Silent Strider will be very different. Tribal culture is much more defined, while a pack culture is very dependent on how its members choose to define themselves and honor their totem.<br /> <br /> Stag as a Garou pack totem is certainly is not limited to the Dark Ages setting. I don't know where you got that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T11:17:51-07:00","id":1384453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384337#post1384337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I was peeved that was never really fleshed out. I mean we get some stuff about Fianna and Fiona being allies, but say Dark Age Werewolf/Fae it didn't make any sort of sense how the Fianna had a fey history when the Dark Age Fae book was all LOL we tricked some werewolves into helping one of our gang fights what rubes!</div> </div> </div> </div>Many sourcebooks had topics that were often only generically addressed, or key points entirely ignored. The ban for packs of Stag to aid the fae existed since the first Werewolf corebook. It was one of those obvious crossover hooks planted in the early days like Malkavians and the fae, or Giovanni and Silent Striders and Wraith. But the game never properly developed guidelines on how that was supposed to happen.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason is that as time went by, the World of Darkness splintered into feuding Developers, and all the gamelines developed some very antagonistic stances to each other and downplayed any kind of connections.<br /> <br /> I don't do crossover in the sense I don't allow PCs of different types (vampires, werewolves, mages, etc.) together, but I do set my chronicles in an integrated setting where all those elements might be encountered. And the selfsame Fae that Garou may be assisting could be involved in things that don't square perfectly with a Garou's other obligations. So I think now is a good time to discuss that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I like the idea that there is an implied non-aggression pact between packs of Stag and the Fae in general. However, not all Fae are going to be doing things the Garou like. So I don't think being a part of Stag actually means there is complete non-aggression between them and the Fae.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Some Fae may like vampires, or have an enchanted Malkavian at court. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Other Fae might be hanging out at a Glen that some other group of werewolves want as a caern and might attack it (a situation similar to one established in Rage Across New York describing the Catskill Mountains \u2013 home to the story of Rip Van Winkle and the little men playing ninepins.)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Members of the Shadow Court and House Balor might have plots with the Black Spiral Dancers or other Wyrm minions.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\">There may be less horrible, but still troublesome plots of the Fae that negatively effect local Garou or the Garou as a whole. They might be manipulating another Garou. Or maybe they're protective of a mortal that other Garou (or even the pack) want eliminated. How are those conflicts handled by Garou who have the Stag totem?</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So there should be plenty of room for conflict between packs of Stag and the Fae, just like one Fae can opposed one another. In such cases, what are the expectations? Should there be such an implied non-aggression pact? Should there be loopholes or exceptions? Is there a different standard?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">On one hand, there is nothing wrong with commitments that come into conflict. In legend, the hero Cuchulain had a geas to never refused hospitality, but also had another geas to never eat dog meat. At some point, he was forced to violate one of those when he was served dogmeat by the host of the house he was visiting. And sometimes it can be fun to see how the PCs work around conflicting bans. However, players can feel angry if they think they are being screwed over or put in a no win scenario. At the very least, these kinds of conflicts need to be addressed up front so the PCs know what they are getting into, and can make preparations to try to avoid such no-win scenarios.<br /> <br /> (Because of that, I completely throw out the idea that the entire Get of Fenris have a blood oath against all Sidhe. That was something introduced in Changeling, and I think should be an example of &quot;failed&quot; crossover. It was ill considered. It would retroactively ruin the chronicles where Get of Fenris PCs had been in a pack under Stag. So I replace that with the idea that there is one specific House of Sidhe that the Get have sworn revenge on. In my chronicles, this is the &quot;House of Vanin&quot; who are enemies because they made alliance with the All High (the Gangrel vampire who is basically Odin). That house replaces the similar House Aesin. I changed the name because if you are going to have a Changeling noble house based on the Norse, it should really be named after the Vanir, not the Aesir.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">I like the idea that dealing with the Fae can be treacherous, and that their interests may not square with the Garou. There is an element of fun with that. But I don't want to set up the PCs to fail, be betrayed, or \u2013 worse - get upset in real life. What's a good balance that is fun to play out?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-29-2020, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T11:51:53-07:00","id":1384464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384444#post1384444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stag as a pack totem is found in every Werewolf corebook going back to first edition. It's a basic part of the game. One of that totem's bans is a requirement to help fae in need. But that's about all there is. There isn't much more description, or other details on how such packs should be run (but that is the case for all pack totems, there's only a few paragraphs description). If you don't have the Werewolf corebook, you can probably find the totem write up somewhere on the internet. There's lot of ongoing or former online games that reference them.<br /> <br /> The Fianna tribebook, which deals with a tribe of Garou with Stag as the tribal totem, has more detail on culture and some Fae interactions. That can be used as partial inspiration, but packs and tribes of the same totem aren't identical. The Fianna tribe versus a a pack of Stag comprising Uktena, Wendigo, and Red Talons, or a pack of Stag with a Get of Fenris, Shadow Lord, and Silent Strider will be very different. Tribal culture is much more defined, while a pack culture is very dependent on how its members choose to define themselves and honor their totem.<br /> <br /> Stag as a Garou pack totem is certainly is not limited to the Dark Ages setting. I don't know where you got that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I see, I just read a passing line in a post below yours mentioning dark ages and I somehow thought this might be related to dark ages fae instead of CTD.<br /> I've read some things about werewolf but never read the core books from beginning to end, so that's why a probably missed the stag totem for so long.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384444#post1384444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I like the idea that dealing with the Fae can be treacherous, and that their interests may not square with the Garou. There is an element of fun with that. But I don't want to set up the PCs to fail, be betrayed, or \u2013 worse - get upset in real life. What's a good balance that is fun to play out?</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You probably already know you should take things I say with a grain of salt, since I was kinda lost in this discussion in the beginning. But I think the mood of treacherous vows is really the best one to give in a game where changelings are the mysterious and foreign beings.<br /> <br /> I think the best way to solve these kind of problems is being subtle. Fae world is all about getting your way while still abiding by the rules. One of Fae traditions is to give hospitality, if a fae who is a known nuisance request hospitality then there is no way to refuse, but the host can make it so the hospitality is very uncomfortable &quot;you see you see, in this house we have a tradition of only eating a single biscuit as meal per day&quot; but then he go outside (while the guest presumably can't since he asked for protection for a reason) and eat while the guest starve. This and many other ways can be used for a Fae to abide by the rules and still have his way.<br /> <br /> The pack might to learn how to do it to given enough interactions, maybe even learn it the hard way. But let's say the shadow court want your help to protect a vampire who is being hunted by the other garous. The pack can instead of fighting make a agreement &quot;hey don't destroy this vampire right know, it's hard to explain, but trust me, we will say exactly where he will be later, I promise&quot;, this way they can fullfill their request of protecting the vampire that one time, but then after there is no more vows attached help their garou brothers. Something along these lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T00:48:16-07:00","id":1384592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384348#post1384348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one thing that can be useful is considering which fae have ties to Stag. This is largely those tied to celtic/gaelic Europe which represents most standard kiths, alongside certain kiths especially such as Sidhe of House Fiona who have the most blatant and obvious ties to the Fianna.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for the ban to work, that it has to apply to all Fae and there needs to be some universal ways for fae and those Garou packs to work. It has to be much more on an ad hoc basis since there isn't some dispatcher coordinating all these packs of Stag, unlike tribal relations with the Fae that the Fianna have and their specific historical ties that develop because of the institutional longevity of the tribe.<br /> <br /> I think most concepts can be effectively reskinned regardless of how the invisible little people are portrayed.<br /> <br /> I really dislike the way modern notions of multiculturalism has seeped into the game. Spirits and such don't care about that. So Stag should have been just as active as a totem in the New World before Columbus as it was in the Old World. Just because there was no Fianna in North America doesn't mean Stag wasn't active there. Just like the lack of a tribe of Boar, Raven, or Bear didn't mean Garou couldn't have those as pack totems. Certain totems may have different cultural baggage in different places, but that's OK. In a game I ran in historical Europe, I used the Uktena totem for an NPC pack, but it was simply known as the Horned Serpent. It wasn't a well known totem, and it didn't have any North American specific mythology behind it, but it was known to the Celtic and Germanic peoples and had the same general mythic resonance (mysterious, occult) as normal.<br /> <br /> And I didn't like how all the worldwide versions of the Fae were effectively different. I think all these Fae should be part of one continuum. That the cultural differences should be a result of different interpretations by humanity. But any differences would be considered to be unimportant reskinnings to the fae themselves. These kinds of stories are universal.<br /> <br /> So I'm not worried about any cultural ties to Celtic Europe. If I was running a game with Uktena and Wendigo pack of Stag, I'd just use my books on Indian legends as more inspiration than my books on European legends. And if needed, I could run a blend of European and Indian legends on the &quot;little people&quot; together. Mortal dreams may reskin them differently, but they're essentially the same people. It's just a matter of how you portray the mixing so that it appears interesting, cool, and mysterious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T23:55:14-07:00","id":1384790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384348#post1384348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Changeling seers and scribes are a strong way for the changelings to discover packs. This might be alongside generational contacts between the changelings and the Fianna, as well as that many changeling hotspots are likely to shine like beacons to garou with the Sense Wyld gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a good way, and it makes the initial contact between a pack of Stag and the fae very court centric. Commoner fae could also have made contact independently, but I think an official meeting would be necessary at some point.<br /> <br /> Are there guidelines on the typical size of a faerie court through the feudal hierarchy (baronies, counties, duchies, kingdoms, high kings)? In terms of the number of fae and various chimerical creatures, what would they be? That would tell me how I should describe the initial (and subsequent) encounters held at the court after a fae messenger summons the pack to meet the local lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T06:23:45-07:00","id":1384830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae#post1384313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I am doing research to help me figure out some ways to include a Garou pack with the Stag totem in the world of the Fae. This is for a Werewolf game, but I wanted to get insight from players of Changeling.This is specifically about Garou packs with the Stag totem, which is something I have not found specifically mentioned in Changeling books. The only Garou references I find are vague generalities concerning tribes. But packs of Stag have a concrete ban involving aiding the Fae so it is something that should be explored in more detail.<br /> <br /> Looking for feedback here on how well you think this could be incorporated from a Changeling specific. In other words, rather than how to fit Changelings into Werewolf, I am wondering how a Changeling game would handle a Garou pack of Stag as a normal part of their setting. While not all domains of Changeling would have a local pack of Stag to call upon, it should be common enough that a sizable minority would have access to one. I can then work back as needed to determine how it appears from a Garou perspective for a Werewolf game.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If there are parts people disagree with, or believe new parts should be added for consideration, let's hear them and the reasons why.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, this is excellent. I often overlap elements of Changeling and Werewolf, so this speaks to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>SHAPECHANGERS AND THE FAE</b><br /> The way I handle Shapechangers and the fae is pretty much how you have detailed. Fianna will often have a pact of mutual aid with the local fae. Fae courts will often have Fianna representatives at court, though such persons are usually Kinfolk who have receives the Ritual of Parted Mists (permanent enchantment). Having fianna packs watching the borderlands of fae territory is a great way to portray this relationship. Fae assistance for the garous should not be underscored- fae can be very potent combatants, and their magical powers are potentially <u>very</u>scary. Fae nobles should be Inhumanly beautiful and having <i><u>seemingly </u></i>limitless magic.<br /> <br /> Other shapeshifters are also frequent visitors, especially Celican were-cats, Corax were-ravens and Nuwisha were-coyotes. Less often seen, but still present are Kitsune werefox\u2019s, Pumonca were-puma, Qualmi were-lynx\u2019s and Black Spiral Dancers (Shadow court only).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TOTEMS AND THE FAE</b><br /> Along with Stag, there are many Incarna spirits with ties to the fae. From a Changeling perspective, I treat such spirits as the true fae dream lords known as the Oneiroi. If they can be personal totems, I am open to fae serving some of these spirits rather than a fae house (buying dots in Totem instead of Rank), but can never accept ranks in a Noble House as a result.<br /> Some totems that I use, with solid fae ties are:<br /> <b>Bacchus </b>(Dionysus)- This ancient Incarna of intoxication, sex and fertility is very old and powerful. Considered an ally by Black Furies and Satyrs (who claim he is an Unseelie fae, and the father of their kith), this entity is also respected by Fianna, Glass Walkers and some Malkavian Vampires.<br /> <b>Balor </b>(Rorq, Incarnae of the Asteroid Belt)- Though defeated by Lugh of the Long Arm in ancient times, this Nightmare Incarnae is still around. The Sidhe of House Balor, Thallain, Unseelie Kithain, and Red Talons all have deep ties with this entity. Balor cannot be taken as a personal totem. Registers as a Incarna servant of the Wyrm of Balance or a really angry Wyld Incarna.<br /> <b>Coyote </b>(Nuwisha)- Coyote is a totem spirit of Cunning, and also the patron of the Nuwisha shapechangers. Among the fae, the Canotili, Eshu, Nanehi, Pooka, and Satyrs kiths are the most likely to have ties with Coyote. Coyote cannot be taken as a totem by fae, though he generally likes fae.<br /> <b>Pan </b>(<a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pan_(Totem)\" target=\"_blank\">Kokopelli</a>)- Pan is the Dancer and the Lover. Black Furies, Kachina, Nuwisha, Pumonca, Uktena, Satyrs and Surem all have deep ties with this totem. Pan makes for an excellent personal totem for Kithain.<br /> <b>Loki </b>\u2013 This fiery and argumentative Incarna is considered a troublemaker by shapechangers and fae alike, but he is a powerful, if quixotic, ally. Get of Fenris, Nuwisha, Redcaps, Sidhe of House Aesin, and Trolls have ties with Loki, though few serve this spirit directly.<br /> <b>Oghma </b>\u2013 One of the Tuatha De Dannan, this Incarna is called the Bard and the Judge. Celican, Fianna, Nuwisha, and all Kithain have deep ties with this spirit. However, this spirit can only be bonded with through roleplaying.<br /> <b>Raven </b>\u2013 This Incarna is well known among the fae. Though greatly respected, this totem does not take fae followers. Raven is most widely acknowledged by Nunnehi, Crow or Raven Pooka, Redcaps, Wendigo, Uktena and Fianna.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-30-2020, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:16:10-07:00","id":1384890,"title":"","content":"Are the Fae Oneiri the same as the normal Oneiri (Dreamlords) like Chimera? I have to ask because sometimes the different World of Darkness lines use the same terms to talk about different concepts, or use different terms to reference the same.<br /> <br /> A while ago I tried to find references to specific Dreamlords, but besides Chimera I could only find a reference in the Book of Worlds to &quot;Myathia of the Twelve Collars&quot; and that was it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:42:30-07:00","id":1384913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384890#post1384890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Fae Oneiri the same as the normal Oneiri (Dreamlords) like Chimera? I have to ask because sometimes the different World of Darkness lines use the same terms to talk about different concepts, or use different terms to reference the same.<br /> <br /> A while ago I tried to find references to specific Dreamlords, but besides Chimera I could only find a reference in the Book of Worlds to &quot;Myathia of the Twelve Collars&quot; and that was it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terms do get awfully jumbled.<br /> <br /> The <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oneiroi to which I am referencing are mysterious entities that are mentioned in a few places, mostly in reference to the Dream Zone, Maya, etc. The Book of Worlds mentions them in passing, referring to them as &quot;god like&quot; in their own dream worlds. Not even the Dreamspeakers have a firm grasp on their nature. They are mentioned in a few Changeling products I believe, perhaps in articles on the Scathach Sidhe, but I am uncertain. This is all mysterious on purpose.<br /> <br /> I treat them as Umbrood/Incarna spirits as the Dreaming perceives them. The various aspects of the Umbra (dreaming included) being distinguished by perception rather than geography. So Balor is a Fomorian giant in the Deep Dreaming, the Incarnae of the Asteroid belt in the Deep Umbra, and other names in other realms. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Powerful true fae could definitely fit into this category, especially the Tuatha. Changelings are far less potent, fettered as they are to time and matter. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:54:22-07:00","id":1384916,"title":"","content":"Next question - what are good kinds of Changeling foes that would make good targets for these Garou? I've found the Creeping Fear (chimerical spiders) as a good choice. And I have various fairy tales and legends to go by. But I am interested in other specific Changeling enemies that are statted up in existing sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> I have players who are very big into Changeling, so the more official lore I can bring into the chronicle the happier I can make them. Since I have made changes to my depiction of the Fae to fit my personal vision and align them better to real world legendry, I know the more WoD references I can use, the more it'll help them adjust to the changes by making it seem more like &quot;home&quot; to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:35:43-07:00","id":1384942,"title":"","content":"A great deal of fun may be had with villains. Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Wyrm Cults- Just as there are Totems allied to the Fianna and the fae, so are there dark totems who serve the Elder Dark. And such entities have their followers among twisted mortals, shapeshifters and dark fae (see below). A cult dedicated to G'lough (aka <a href=\"http://mundotentacular.blogspot.com/2018/09/shub-niggurath-dark-mother-and-mythos.html\" target=\"_blank\">Shub Niggurath</a>), Fachan (an elder Redcap god) or even Qyrl (aka Cthulhu) are all possible. Most of these cults could just be mortal creeps without powers or enchanted by a fae leader, mortal sorcerer or Black Spiral Dancer. Fomori may result from such cults.<br /> <br /> Night Hags- Called Nocturnae by the Garou, these awful Thallain are particularly nasty opponents. These evil fae are all about tormenting dreams and sucking the life out of their prey through dreams and night visits. And if the hag is experienced, they might be quite powerful. A whole chronicle might revolve around a Hag or group of them and chimera servitors preying on children, etc. <br /> <br /> Autumn People- Banal people looking to &quot;clean up&quot; the area by destroying a place of natural or artistic splendor. This will destroy a place of mystical significance and chase away any Glamour. The local fae and shapechangers must work together. Autumn people are VERY banal, and difficult for the fae to deal with directly, but going in there are ripping them to shreds is not a good idea either. So some finesse is needed.<br /> <br /> Banes, etc- Many banes overlap with Nightmare chimera, but are not always the same thing. They feed on negative emotions, negative fantasies and such, and so the difference could be splitting hairs. In my games I treat many Banes as corrupted Chimera, gaining a boost from linking with the Wyrm, but becoming increasingly foul because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-30-2020, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T17:32:48-07:00","id":1384965,"title":"","content":"Skinwalkers would make a good enemy too. They are thallain changeling, but also shapeshifters, who can turn into the animal they have killed off. I think the rules only talk about common animals, but would be interesting if they could turn into other things as well, specially if you want to power up one.<br /> If the game is in USA, they are also deep connected with native lore. I can be a great mindfuck to players. They might belive a skinwalker can only be something that is associated with their world, but they are fae.<br /> <br /> <br /> Drones (possessed by Weaver spirits) Could also be specially awful autumm people, once they connect with the onesong they basically become cleaner of anything supernatural, extremely prejudicial to myths and glamour. They basically are there to assure humanity forget anything that could make them belive there is omething magical or supernatural in the world.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 04-30-2020, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T19:03:05-07:00","id":1384982,"title":"","content":"Alrighty so let's see...<br /> <br /> \u2022Courts<br /> The Kithain court system does maintain a size of feudalism ranging from Households-Kingdoms although the specifics of those populations for both kithain and chimera is ultimately left to Storytellers. It's also probably important to note that many commoner freeholds would likely have the more longstanding ties with the Fianna and Stag packs given the Sidhe's return in 1969.<br /> <br /> \u2022Totems &amp; Fae<br /> -I will admit that I really like some of these totem-far relationship ideas and I can see how the totems might have corresponding avatars in the Dreaming. My main reservation though is considering how the Dreaming-Umbra avatars interact with one another and the meta-cosmological ties between the totems of the Middle Umbra and the chimera of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> \u2022Enemies of Stag<br /> -A big determining factor is whether or not the Garou of Stag have been enchanted, but I'll assume they have been. Given that most Stag garou are probably aligned to the Dreaming via their changeling allies, which means that thallain and nightmare chimera are gonna be some of their biggest chimerical threats. Also those garou who make a point of combatting the Weaver would probably make a similar point of fighting Autumn People, dauntain, and other agents of banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T06:49:56-07:00","id":1385070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384982#post1384982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022Totems &amp; Fae<br /> -I will admit that I really like some of these totem-far relationship ideas and I can see how the totems might have corresponding avatars in the Dreaming. My main reservation though is considering how the Dreaming-Umbra avatars interact with one another and the meta-cosmological ties between the totems of the Middle Umbra and the chimera of the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I so enjoy your posts.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is all my own wandering thoughts. And something I fall back on when running mixed troupe games. I don't mean to say that &quot;all are one and the same,&quot; but rather that differing avatars of Incarna are pieces of the puzzle, or </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">variations of the same story</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> (like how Beauty and the Beast is a retelling of Cupid and Psyche). Not that everyone works well together, there might even be disagreements with different aspects of the same being. For storytelling purposes, I would say that the Dreaming aspect of a Totem is the &quot;story-book&quot; version of these entities. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For example;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> the totem Fenris might have an aspect of the Big Bad Wolf in the Dreaming, who is still </span>damned scary,</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> but not the mind blasting monster revered by the Get of Fenris. You could say the Big Bad Wolf is a &quot;pup&quot; of the Fenris, but still a possible route to connect with the Great Wolf. Asking the Big Bad Wolf to lead you to his &quot;fathers den&quot; sounds like an awesome quest.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Some totems fit better in the &quot;fairy tale&quot; realm of the Dreaming. But I could definitely see many of them hanging out in the Dreaming more than the Umbra. Bacchus, Pan, Unicorn, Pegasus, etc. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 05-01-2020, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T13:47:53-07:00","id":1385132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1384982#post1384982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-A big determining factor is whether or not the Garou of Stag have been enchanted, but I'll assume they have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly an option, but I don't think the only one for packs of Stag. Werewolf has always had penumbral domains of Trods which are associated with the Fae. They aren't the same thing as trods in Changeling, but do seem to map to the Green Paths of Balor. So I think Garou can independently enter the Dreaming. Of course, they would normally get easily lost. However, I think the totem avatar in Stag should be more helpful in this regard compared to other pack totems. And packs can always build their totems to have the Sense Airt charm, which should allow them to follow spirit paths. As an ST, this is something that I'd allow that the more XP put into Totem Background should mean a more knowledgeable guide along the Fae trods - at least on the Green Paths of Balor, but at high levels at least the other trods in the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow them to see Fae mien and such in the Realm unless they were Enchanted or similar powers were involved.<br /> <br /> Interested in hearing comments on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that most Stag garou are probably aligned to the Dreaming via their changeling allies, which means that thallain and nightmare chimera are gonna be some of their biggest chimerical threats. Also those garou who make a point of combatting the Weaver would probably make a similar point of fighting Autumn People, dauntain, and other agents of banality. </div> </div> </div>Can you give specific examples/descriptions of the type of creatures Thallain and Nightmare Chimera represent? I'm looking for actual ideas to portray at players, and I'm just not familiar enough with these terms to have specifics in mind. For example, I know the Creeping Fear are giant spiders. What other specific creatures are there?<br /> <br /> I know only a little about people like Autumn People and Dauntain. From what I understand, while they're incredibly dangerous to Changelings, they'd just be normal people from a Garou perspective. So while the Garou would certainly be great help against them from a Changeling perspective, I think it would be a very minor thing for Garou except that it could lead to a few interesting scenes as to how to deal and interact with a psychologist at an institution, or an overly strict schoolteacher and the like. A nice quiet scene or two over the course of a chronicle, but not something I think most players would want to concentrate on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T14:23:33-07:00","id":1385137,"title":"","content":"Dauntain are twisted Changelings and thoroughly bad news.<br /> <br /> Autumn people are effectively Weaver corrupted humans. Not a direct threat to Garou, but are likely to have patter spider shadows.<br /> <br /> Thallain are dark fae. The sort that would hang out with Black Spiral Dancers. Every dark faerie creature you can think of fits the bill. Child eating hags, the scissorman, rawhead and bloody bones. Get ffreaky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 05-01-2020, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T17:43:54-07:00","id":1385157,"title":"","content":"\u2022Totem &amp; Dreaming Synergy<br /> -Yeah, I lean towards something along those lines myself. Something between the concept of a sort of Ur-Dream akin to the Proto-Indo European culture/mythology/language that some academics spend their careeets trying to reconstruct and a sort of 'white light through a prism' situation where these all originate from the same central cosmic Concept but have been refracted into several different wavelengths. (Also, thank ya Myth Advocate, your posts are cool as well!)<br /> <br /> \u2022Trods &amp; Dreaming Roads<br /> -I definitely agree that what many garou describe as umbral trods, particularly pocket realms tied to Dreaming individuals, are likely analogous to the various roads that changelings use to maneuver. To expand on tries though, some potentially interesting things:<br /> <br /> --Trods each have their own unique methods of access. While the vast majority of freeholds contain trods that access the Near Dreaming and trods close to The Waking World (mundane reality) have less extreme codes, all trods have a code. The details are sky as the limit; some simply require an introductory poem to be recited, others only allow you to continue by walking back, others will have you accosted by riddling chimera; no trod is alike and refusal to play by The Dreaming's rules is a fast lane to an... interesting life.<br /> --Trods entering the Far Dreaming tend to be even more difficult, requiring traveler's to observe ritualistic conditions and submit themselves to the esoteric logic of dreams. Access to the Deep Dreaming is even more difficult, often requiring either truly prodigious circumstances or an extreme sacrifice such as a significant treasure or a great tribute of glamour.<br /> --Trods often simply appear as narratively appropriate (both in and out of universe) although the rise of banality weakens them and many were lost in great cataclysms. Other ways to access these roads are through the use of considerable Wayfarer, the services a proficient dream-sorcerer (Oneiromancy) capable of physically traveling via dreams, or having the sheer luck (or lack there of...) to randomly chance upon a Wild Portal. Along with all of this, one should note that trods are invaluable military assets within the Dreaming and treated as such by changelings and chimera, although fae military procedure is sometimes rather eccentric when compared to The Nation.<br /> --There are also Three Roads specifically which are invaluable to safely travel the Dreaming. The Silver Road was established by the Tuatha and is of Dreams, with those of Nightmare pained by contact with it due to the ancient Silver Ban. The Paths of Balor are the elder equivalent of the Silver Road claimed by the children of the Elder Dark and with Paths reaching throughout the Dreaming, Shadowlands, and Autumn World. The Twilight Trods are fiercely contested because they can be used by either side, being largely rebuilt Post-Shattering. <br /> <br /> \u2022Nightmare &amp; The Elder Dark<br /> -Thallain, Nightmare Chimera, and other Children of the Elder Dark are those glamorous beings who declare fealty to the primordial terrors of the world's beginning, the Nightmare and Elder Dark. They feed from the worst aspects of human passion and their nightmares; ranging from reaping sorrow or provoking bloodshed to feed upon terror, hatred, and desperation. They are, by their nature, inherently opposed to the Children of the Dreaming. The two factions have fought since humanity achieved higher cognition, or even earlier. They were held distant by The Silver Ban for a long time but the Evanescence in the late 90s and early 2000s saw a massive influx of Nightmare glamour which saw a great surge in thallain numbers. They dream of returning humanity to its base and primordial state, welcoming the Long Winter as that promised return and the death of Dreams. They are, by and large, almost certainly tied to the Wyrm, particularly thallain who are the debased little siblings of the Dark Kin.<br /> <br /> \u2022Agents of Autumn <br /> -Autumn People &amp; Dauntain probably would register highly as normal people, being difficult to detect unless one is closely tied to glamour, but those with high gnosis or Sense Weaver would almost certainly sense such individuals. They represent the agents of Banality, the slow and crushing destruction of Dreams under the weight of sheer and unrelenting apathy, disappointment, and emotional numbing. They are arguably an even greater threat to the Fae of the Dreaming then the thallain, particularly since they are far more insidious in human society. Autumn People aren't cackling satanists or sadists. They're bitter school intendents who cut funding to the arts and aloof passerby who make a point of tipping the street busker but only to condescendingly tell him to 'get a real job'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T23:27:54-07:00","id":1385201,"title":"","content":"Another question for the setting. What should Garou look like when they are in the Dreaming? Should they look as they normally do in whatever form they are in? Or should they look subtly changed so that it is obvious they are werewolves? For example, maybe in homid form they look hairier than normal with unkempt hair, more pronounced fangs, and perhaps even a change in eye color? And in lupus they'd appear bulkier as their mouths slaver, and their eyes have a demonic look to them? Something that obvious marks them as a Prodigal rather than an Enchanted human or trespassing Mage?<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been thinking on my own of the kinds of monsters to include for Garou to deal with. I don't want Garou packs of Stag to be seen as someone who deals with &quot;ordinary&quot; threats to the Fae, though they still could in any given situation. I want to keep the idea that they're a kind of military reserve to be called out when things get really bad or out of the ordinary. So I was thinking a good idea may be when the Fae are fighting something &quot;not native to Earth's Dreaming&quot; but something that wandered out of Lovecraft's Dreamlands or Dunsany's Pegana. It's <i>fairy-like,</i> but not a creature you'd expect the read about in a fairy tale.<br /> <br /> Examples would be creatures like Nightgaunts, Moonbeasts, Gugs, and Serpent Men although I'd need to file all the serial #s off and reimagine them in way that better fits the cosmology of the World of Darkness. Nightgaunts are easy because I can simply have them be heralds, messengers, and agents of the Elder Dark. The representatives they send to the Shadow Court and Thallain. In Lovecraft's Mythos, Serpent Men in the Dreamlands were once creatures of the real world who moved there through psychic or sorcerous powers to escape their race's decline on Earth. I usually use the Vhujunka as my serpent men analogue in Werewolf games, so I could do the same here. Despite including one Vhujunka in most of my chronicles as a sandbox element, I've never yet had PCs run into them. So this actually may be a better opportunity to do so.<br /> <br /> I have to do a lot more thinking on Moonbeasts though. They're actually one of the most malevolent races in the Dreamlands and sufficiently alien to make them interesting antagonists in the Dreaming. But I don't think I can tie them to the moon. Not only would that not make sense from a Garou perspective since Luna is an important patron of them, the moon's correspondence to Arcadia in Changeling also makes it bad fit. I think I need some other kind of celestial correspondence. Perhaps they are like an &quot;Eclipse Beast&quot;? Moonbeasts are sadists and slavers, and have agents among the Men from Leng. So they too would make great behind-the-scenes masterminds using secret agents among the Shadow Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T02:46:35-07:00","id":1385224,"title":"","content":"<br /> Alien and primordial Dreams are great as dangers and antagonists. <br /> <br /> Moon beasts (or whatever you call them) would make for great Dreaming monsters. I would say they would worship the Elder Dark. And I dont think the Moon needs to be left out. The Black Spiral Dancers still revere Luna, and haven't lost her favor.<br /> <br /> As for Garou in the Dreaming- I would go with wolf tropes like unibrows and hairy palms. Some features based on breed may come into play, like Homid looking at best like Glabro, Lupus looking like Hispo and Metic looking like Crinos, maybe even having that be a Garou's base form while in the Dreaming. <br /> Fianna would get an Irish legend look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 05-02-2020, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T16:02:19-07:00","id":1385314,"title":"","content":"Aye, moonbeasts and alien dreams make great Changeling-style antagonists. The Dreaming is every dream and so it makes sense that the eldritch horrors that are dreamed by things we don't understand would be horrors there.<br /> <br /> As far as the chimerical aspect of werewolves, there will definitely be a great deal of diversity. In a way, I'd say that Breed-Auspice-Tribe can all serve as ways to provide unique factors to them alongside universal features akin to the Tells of Wolf-Blooded in WtF.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that the level of the Dreaming is important to recall. The Near Dreaming is similar to The Waking World, except that the mien gains prominence and stands upfront in reality. The Far Dreaming intensifies things as archetypes gain more and more potency. The Deep Dreaming is a realm defined by Archetype and Primal Dream, where Jumgian Archetypes, Mythic Legends, and The Heroes Journey reside as measurable foundations of reality.<br /> <br /> For example two random garou in the Near Dreaming might manifest greater body hair, bestial eyes, or attract animal followers. Similarly homids might see their fingers change sizes or lupus might be hulking big bad wolves or metis might be slick with birth blood and placenta. A Black Fury might find themselves clad in laurels or that chimerical steeds make a point of approaching them while a Fianna might find their voice gaining an ethereal quality and that the landscape itself wants to dance and sing with them.<br /> <br /> The same characters in the Far Dreaming might find the landscape shifting to resemble a graecian temple or hibernian glade. Ancestral relics akin to voile might manifest or the garou feel primordial instincts rising to the fore. Ragabash might literally vanish from sight while stepping into shadows or Ahroun might shine with a penumbra of moonlight.<br /> <br /> With The Dreaming, imagination and intent are really the only mitigating factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T17:18:57-07:00","id":1385326,"title":"","content":"Perhaps if I say they come from the Dark Side of the Moon, that'd be sufficient, and call them Dark Siders for short. That would keep the moon connection, but since people on Earth can never see the far side of the moon, it also represents an unknown land. And since a moon connection would implies ties to space, I could link other creatures similar to the Greys who supposedly contact and abduct people. As many have noted, these stories have many similarities to stories about faerie kidnappings and such.<br /> <br /> Going back to the idea that the pack's totem avatar could help his Garou navigate the Dreaming. What ideas do you have on using the pack totem avatar as an NPC in the Dreaming? How much information should they know? Like should they essentially have an extent of knowledge equal to the corebook? Less? More? How should the inhabitants of the Dreaming treat or interact with the totem avatar? The Garou are just Garou, but the totem avatar is a spirit avatar of Stag himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T23:10:06-07:00","id":1385356,"title":"","content":"Heck the Dark Side of the Moon makes sense to me, that sounds pretty solid and interesting. Along with that might be things from beyond the stars or below in sea or stone where light never touches.<br /> <br /> \u2022Aliens &amp; Fae<br /> -Oh yeah definitely. Dreams are eternal but their images can take on plenty of different forms. Plus extraterrestrials have managed to insert a strong significance into certain sorts of dreams such as fear and fascination with the unknown so the idea of flying disks or chimerical grays wandering mysterious stretches of chimerical reality is perfectly plausible. Plus plenty of arts and enchanting 'abduction' can have solid analogues.<br /> <br /> \u2022Totems in the Dreaming<br /> -I'm... genuinely uncertain about this. Because I can see the logic and get the use of having a pack totem join the pack entering the Dreaming. I guess my problem is, I think that the Dreaming and Umbra are on different wavelengths and for spirits of one to pass into the others... if it's possible, I don't think it should be an easy undertaking. Spirits are manifestations of that realm's foundational energies come to life and while the human world is a universal constant, realms built upon completely distinct energies can't be easy on outsiders.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd say that for totems such as Stag that do have ties to fae elements, I'd say that they probably have contacts and allies bound by old oaths in the Dreaming who could serve as guides or mentors to their packs, although they probably also have rivals and sworn enemies. Stag for instance might be allied with The Horned Lord, The White Hart and able to secure numerous chimerical deer and hunters to help their packs. Yet they might also constantly draw the ire of cruel hunters and ravenous nightmares, such as rabid bears or sadistic trappers or even simple grass-lings (tiny people) that begrudge Stag's proud hooves trodfing through their villages.<br /> <br /> As for some of your other questions: I'd say that a totem does probably have some of its incarna's knowledge with its totem value and the points into it expanding its knowledge but suffer from some key misconceptions simply due to the difference in nature of umbral spirits and dreamt chimera and their minds. They likely recall past experiences and know basics such as the names of allies and enemies as well as how to pass through certain ways and the capabilities of certain chimera, but the intent and reasons of much of the Dreaming probably baffles them. Akin to that, aspects of the Dreaming can only interact with the spirit as far as they can understand and interpret it. Chimerical deer might mostly understand but not get why Stag allows its children to be hunted and killed. Alternatively chimerical hunters might happily hunt any Stag, regardless of its significance. Or as well a daydream might simply not understand in the slightest what any particular spirit is trying to say at all.<br /> <br /> Most chimera and changelings probably don't have spirit speech or an equivalent. They have no reason to. Spirits are animist reflections of reality. Chimera are human dreams inspired by reality, sometimes very loosely. They interact on different levels. They might be able to comprehend each other's existence but it's... no sure thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T01:19:37-07:00","id":1385376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1385356#post1385356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most chimera and changelings probably don't have spirit speech or an equivalent. They have no reason to. Spirits are animist reflections of reality. Chimera are human dreams inspired by reality, sometimes very loosely. They interact on different levels. They might be able to comprehend each other's existence but it's... no sure thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was originally thinking that as &quot;part of the Umbra - aka not the Realm&quot; that the pack totem avatar would appear in the Dreaming like it would in the Penumbra or other Middle Umbra realm (like Arcadia Gateway). But now I'm wondering if that might not actually be the case. Their totem avatar could lead them to a trod where they could pass into the Dreaming, but then wouldn't show up in the Dreaming because it's ephemeral but not chimerical.<br /> <br /> The Garou would still have access to their Totem like they normally do - still use any of its powers, and if they selected the right totem powers even speak to it, But their pack totem would not be &quot;physically&quot; present.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know if there were ever rules explaining how Garou and their totems work in the Dreaming?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T04:55:29-07:00","id":1385387,"title":"","content":"I would say that Stag and many other totem avatars would show up normally in the dreaming. Its all ephemera, just different &quot;flavors.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T12:01:08-07:00","id":1385440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1385387#post1385387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that Stag and many other totem avatars would show up normally in the dreaming. Its all ephemera, just different &quot;flavors.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would tend to agree. Stag and his brood especially, but I'd argue that any spirit would just appear as they are in the Dreaming because there's not a separate intangible state there - it's all ephemera as matter. <br /> <br /> Also, per the Changeling Book of Storyteller Secrets, many of the gifts that worked on spirits in the parallel Werewolf edition (probably 2nd, but many of those still exist) would work on chimerical entities, though some require the werewolf to be enchanted. That implies that the two are cousins in a way, and in a given realm (Dreaming or Umbra), the visiting variety will appear according to similar rules as per the native kind - in the Dreaming spirits will appear according to the same rules as chimera, and in the Umbra, Chimera will appear as spirits do. This is backed up by the Mage section, which puts chimerical interactions under the Spirit sphere.<br /> <br /> That book also states that enchantment only costs one glamour to enchant &quot;any garou in sight&quot; (the wording is vague on if this would enchant ALL garou in the line of sight, or if it means they could spend one glamour and enchant any werewolf they see - I believe the latter was the intent), and the enchantment lasts twice as long as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T15:13:28-07:00","id":1385467,"title":"","content":"For the sake of theme and storytelling, the Dreaming avatar for Stag should have a powerful, &quot; storybook&quot; feel. Such as a huge White Stag / Lord of the Forest type of being","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T17:57:30-07:00","id":1385491,"title":"","content":"There may be some 20th edition rules in the Umbra W20 as to how garou would deal with being in realms of dreams.<br /> <br /> It does also come to an extent down to how you as ST want to handle the situation because as you can see from this thread there are different perspectives on how the spirits of the middle umbra might interact with the chimera of the dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:59:55-07:00","id":1385522,"title":"","content":"Everyone convinced me my first notion was correct - the pack's totem avatar should be &quot;physically&quot; present in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> I notice that the Changeling books have some examples of actual Oaths that can be sworn, and then the mechanical effects of that. Does anyone have suggestions as to an appropriate &quot;Oath&quot; that new packs of Stag may make when they first pledge themselves to Stag that would happen before Stag's ban takes effect? I think it would be an interesting touch to show them the importance of Oaths in Fae society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:29:54-07:00","id":1387062,"title":"","content":"I found examples of published Oaths online and used them to cobble together a pseudo-Oath for packs of Stag. Something they'd say during their totem quest and winning Stag's favor.<br /> <br /> I call it a pseudo-oath because it is not actually a Changeling style oath, but accepting a totem ban. Any violations of it would result in the typical Garou chiminage relations to spirits, not the Dreaming reality kicking in. I wanted to keep Garou agency but with the surface of a fae type Oath.<br /> <br /> This is what I came up with:<br /> <br /> <i>I, (name), pledge to Stag, my Father and Prince of the Forest, to fulfill the ancient pact. What Stag entrusts to my care, I will guard. I will thank all who give me the bounty of their life so I may live. I will rescue the Children of the Earth in need who call on my aid, and stop the depredations of those who would torment them whenever possible. As the sun guards the Earth by day; as the moon by night, so shall I watch over the lands of Dana. Grant me your boon, and I gladly accept this burden. This I swear. May the realm of Arcadia ever look with favor upon my oath.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T16:39:26-07:00","id":1387833,"title":"","content":"I'm looking for some specific help now. I finally found the time to read some more information on the Autumn People and Dauntain. I was actually pleasantly surprised that at the variety of examples of each and their appropriateness. I think there is a lot I can use. For my purposes, I am looking at ways to involve Garou packs of Stag.<br /> <br /> For the Autumn People, I think in general Garou won't be of use. The Garou are a military warband, and aren't really appropriate to sic on the Autumn People. I'm sure there are exceptions, but overall it would be overkill and probably result in more blowback than what it is worth.<br /> <br /> But I think there are some great Dauntain concepts that would work. This is where I'm looking to brainstorm and put some meat on these bones.<br /> <br /> First, I think there's a lot of potential with the Cursed who take the Oath of Undoing against a sworn enemy. I'm thinking of a doomed, tragic figure like Lord Soth in Dragonlance - a fae whose passions doomed them because they gave into hate and vengeance. Someone with nobility who would otherwise be good, but gets sucked into a dark path. Someone I could introduce early in a chronicle as a likable chap. Probably some kind of fae knight or noble that could fill a &quot;black knight&quot; role as he cuts a bloody road in his path of vengeance. An equivalent to a Conan, Ogami Itto, Walker, Bryan Mills, or John Wick. An implacable force of nature whose wielding of banality makes him or her too dangerous for most fae champions, so the local duke or whatever calls in the Garou. Hard thing here is to make a single fae, or perhaps a small band with one main &quot;bad guy&quot; with some helpers, to be a serious challenge for an entire pack.<br /> <br /> Second, the Typhoid concepts work great when the reason is that a Changeling has been ghouled by a Vampire. Perhaps the vampire did or did not know the person was a Changeling, but in any event this would be a great loss to the fae community and is a large risk that it could spread. Again, this is a perfect time for the local Fae to call in the Garou to help. I'm thinking the most likely vampire domitor would be a Toreador or Malkavian, but there are plenty of other concepts that could be appropriate. I need an interesting back story that explains how the vampire's and changeling's paths crossed and eventually lead to the ghouling. And good complications and obstacles the Garou would have to overcome. And there's the issue of whether the Changeling can be redeemed, or whether he will need to be destroyed because he has been corrupted too much.<br /> <br /> Finally, I am thinking of a Nihilist Dauntain, probably someone whose mortal seeming is institutionalized in a psychiatric center. There's some good mirroring of Harano among the Garou, and I can mine that for a lot. This would be more like a rescue mission as opposed to an enemy to be crushed. And I think I can do some interesting things with the Umbra and spirits. I just need some ideas on how such a person can become a major threat to fae so that they need to do something about her as opposed to isolate and leave her alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, outside of the Dauntain, I am thinking about other Enchanted Prodigals to bring to court or a motley gathering in order to create some dilemmas for the pack. What would be some good reasons why a group of fae may want to enchant a Malkavian (or any other concept if you have a good one) vampire? Even assuming the vampire would not be a threat in terms of Banality, there's still a risk in bringing them in conflict. So there'd need to be a good reason. But I like the idea of having an enemy brought into a neutral space where the pack will feel they can't do anything about it. One thing I like to do in games is allow conversations between the PCs and bad guys, but this is often very hard in Werewolf for obvious reasons. But on somewhat neutral ground the pack is pledged to protect, I can finally eat my cake and have it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T00:48:47-07:00","id":1388595,"title":"","content":"In my Head Stag wasn't a Fae Spirit that became an Incarna, Stag was a representative of Nature at the time when the Primordial Fae forged pacts with the living Earth. I would have Stag as an Ally to the Spring Court Fae, who were later remembered as Tuatha. And Stags Tribe would have familial ties with the descendants of a branch of these Spring Fae Nobility, the Fiona.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T22:41:25-07:00","id":1389200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1388595#post1388595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my Head Stag wasn't a Fae Spirit that became an Incarna, Stag was a representative of Nature at the time when the Primordial Fae forged pacts with the living Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is about what I was thinking, but you articulated much better. I'll be taking this wording and using it in-character if I ever need to do some explanations. &quot;When the first Fae forged pacts with the Living Earth, she sent the Prince of the Forest to watch their lands.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T18:40:19-07:00","id":1391091,"title":"","content":"I just had another thought. The legend of the Wild Hunt is an element in both Werewolf and Changeling. In Werewolf, it is a group of spirits - the Wild Huntsman himself and his Hounds. They are the spirits of fury and the instruments of Stag's vengeance. The Fianna can call upon them when in dire peril from a Wyrm menace. This is a Tribal Gift level 5 named Calls the Wild Hunt. Although these have spirit traits, the description says they are a &quot;morass of spiritual energy&quot; rather than specific entities.<br /> <br /> I know the Wild Hunt is mentioned in Changeling, although the mentions I've found are sparse. In real world legend, the Wild Hunt was often made up of ghostly spirits who did not pass onto heaven or hell. In Scottish lore, they were called sluagh, but the game's Sluagh don't meet that definition and aren't involved. However, the Adhene known as the Keremet meet both definitions. They are essentially wraiths captured by Fae or somehow stuck in the Dreaming who then become a type of Adhene, and are mentioned as participants of the Wild Hunt. However, I don't know if the gameline has made any other connections.<br /> <br /> In any case, I think this is something that can be built upon Garou packs of Stag. Their master is Stag. The Wild Hunt is an instrument of Stag's vengeance. Packs of Stag are supposed to be defenders of the fae. And there needs to be some kind of Wild Hunt among the fae.<br /> <br /> So I'm thinking maybe there is an element of the pact that says when a Fae calls the Wild Hunt, that the local packs of Stag are expected to join in. This would be one case where the Garou are compelled to assist. They have no choice. (Although in the Gift Calling the Wild Hunt it says if the gift is used more than once in a month, or if the Hunstman finds the reason to not be worthy, that the spirits attack the Garou instead. So there is likely such an element in the Fae calling packs of Stag to a similar hunt as well. Perhaps being given approval or not by the pack's jaggling avatar.) I don't think such a thing should be issued lightly. So perhaps there is a special order - of fae knights or fae magicians - who know the secrets of Stag's lore that they can call upon the hunt. That compels both packs of Stag and the Keremets to join the Hunt. Perhaps there is a special fae treasure, like a horn when blown, which notifies the local Garou packs of Stag and calls them to fulfill this sacred duty.<br /> <br /> This could be used to send the Hunt to go after terrible things in the Dreaming, or in the mortal world to go after someone who has deeply wronged the fae. Werewolves working under a Fae huntsman (along with the Keremets) to slay or seize someone in the Realm/Waking World would help a lot as it avoids placing the Fae at risk of banality.<br /> <br /> In the Hellboy story King Vold, the Wild Hunt there is lead by King Vold whose hounds are the ghost of Viking Beserkers. Although obviously non-canonical for our purposes, I wanted to point it out as a source that obviously links werewolves with the hounds of the Wild Hunt.<br /> <br /> If anyone has additional information on the Wild Hunt as it relates to Changeling, please post it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 06-14-2020, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T19:32:51-07:00","id":1391106,"title":"","content":"It could be interesting since Fianna don't just have the Wild Hunt summoning gift, they have that Fae Kinship gift that allows them to summon Fae assistance, so its appropriate if it was some sort of mutual agreement. This is interesting when you consider the BSDs and Balor having a similar situation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T20:10:29-07:00","id":1391113,"title":"","content":"You're probably right. In the back of my head, I've had the idea that when the Apocalypse comes, a lot of Fianna are just going to disappear on their fellow Garou because they've been summoned to help kill the Fomorians in the Dreaming as opposed to helping out in the Realm.<br /> <br /> In terms of crossover rules, I believe the game allowed Changelings to roll Willpower to resist the effects of the Faeire Kin gift. So I may allow Garou in Packs of Stag to do likewise. Good call.<br /> <br /> However, for the purposes of this discussion, I think it is important to distinguish between the Fianna and Packs of Stag. The Fianna as a whole don't have the same obligations as packs of Stag. One reason for that, is that in terms of high politics, the Fianna are more like a sovereign nation. The Fae, at high levels, have dealings with the Fianna leadership at high levels. But like NATO or any other alliance, certain legal points need to be invoked in order to mobilize the wheels of high diplomacy. In contrast, packs of Stag (which could be comprised of any tribe) are more like the French Foreign Legion, or perhaps a group of mercenaries hired to do a job. The levels of interaction and mutual obligation are very different.<br /> <br /> Unlike the Fianna tribal gifts, a Pack of Stag may not have access to any of those gifts. It's entirely possible the pack has no Fianna members. (Although as an ST, I would be much more willing to share such tribal gifts as an out-of-auspice/tribe/breed Gift available to pack members because their pack jaggling avatar is of Stag. I'd do the same for any other pack totem. And for pack totems that aren't one of the tribal totems, I'd generate an appropriate list for them). <br /> <br /> So I only want to look at Gifts as inspirations or possible guidelines on how packs of Stag interact with the Fae. I don't want to confuse the Fianna with these Packs of Stag. They're different.<br /> <br /> I know that in Changeling lore, High King David made a pack of Fianna part of the Red Branch Knights. But I'm pretty sure they must have been Fianna who were also a members of a pack of Stag with only Fianna members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T20:29:17-07:00","id":1391121,"title":"","content":"Good point on Pack of Stag not necessarily being Fianna. I always liked having Tribal Totems as Pack Totems for other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T01:12:00-07:00","id":1393034,"title":"","content":"I just had another idea. While Garou and Fae have a long history of cooperation, there are times they've been enemies. And Garou know that certain places controlled by the Fae are potential caerns. (I can't remember if all Freeholds are potential caerns, or if only some of them are, or if it is an entirely different concept in Changeling that could become caerns). [Edit - I now think its Glens that can be turned into caerns). There are other reasons they come into conflict, but I think this would be the biggest one.<br /> <br /> And while I don't know if I'd ever force PCs down this route, it is one with the biggest impact on PC decisions. Because Garou descending upon a Freehold in order to claim it and turn it into a caern is certainly producing Fae in need of help. And a pack of Stag would certainly be useful.<br /> <br /> It could potentially make things worse too as a pack could always decide to violate their Totem ban and join their Garou comrades. But that would have a huge penalty, and one I think that would destroy the pack as I don't see what chiminage the pack members could do to assuage Stag. Still, any Fae who would call upon a pack of Stag better do so after having some knowledge of its member's behaviors, motivations, and likely response. I think most packs of Stag would answer the call and defend the Freehold. It could be like the Magnificent Seven, or the 300 Spartans, or any movie where the cavalry arrives in time to save the day.<br /> <br /> It would definitely make an interesting story, and one that could be a long term payoff as well as disrupting a game that's become predictable and inject new life into it. For there would have to be repercussions.<br /> <br /> Now what tribes would most likely to do so? I think we can safely rule the Fianna out. I think the Black Furies, Children of Gaia, Silent Striders, Stargazers, Uktena, and Wendigo would also not do it. Bone Gnawers aren't ambitious enough to do something like that. That is over half the tribes.<br /> <br /> The Silver Fangs are definitely arrogant to do it in some circumstances. The Shadow Lords are definitely ambitious enough. The Get of Fenris could convince themselves if necessary. I could also see the Glass Walkers trying if they found one in an urban environment. There has to be few urban caerns, and their interests don't make them sympathetic to Fae. As long as the risk-reward ratio works out for them on their spreadsheets, I think they'd be willing to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 06-02-2020, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T22:58:03-07:00","id":1400460,"title":"","content":"I was reading a book on fairy folklore recently and it mentioned reports of &quot;fairy battles&quot;. Usually there was some natural event that reminded people of a battle - such as the color red suddenly appearing in the wilderness (due to a certain kind of fungus or mold) that looked like blood, or mass die off of insects.<br /> <br /> So that sparked a scenario where I think packs of Stag could really come in handy. A time when the Near Dreaming is in constant warfare. So the fae are fighting themselves, and there's lot of warbands and banditry as a result. The fae who are normally keeping the peace are therefore fighting each other. This would be a perfect time for a pack of Stag to keep the peace by fighting other enemies of the local fae, and perhaps defending the commoners from the warbands.<br /> <br /> This may not be something that can be used all the time, but is a good hook for certain occasions if the ST wants a chronicle with heavy crossover elements.<br /> <br /> The chronicle I am currently running takes place during the Interregnum. But now I think a good hook is to refer to the period as The Anarchy, and present it as an era when law and order has really broken down. That will provide lots of hooks for my pack of Stag. The name change obviously comes from English history when the realm of England had two opposing claimants (King Stephen and Queen Matilda). But in terms of inspiration, I am thinking of the legendary tales of England after the death of Uther Pendragon and before Arthur claimed the Sword in the Stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-03-2020, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T15:11:46-07:00","id":1402873,"title":"","content":"I realized that my posts here were concentrated on the Garou-Fae were mostly centered in the Dreaming or otherwise on the home turf of the Fae. However, I neglected to explore what kind of things from a Changeling perspective that Fae might ask Garou to do in the Realm/Autumn World.<br /> <br /> What kind of supernatural menaces might fae want the Garou to take care of for them (as opposed to something they deal with themselves, or ask another Fae to do)?<br /> <br /> What kind of mundane difficulties might the fae ask the Garou to do (as opposed to doing themselves, or asking one of the Enchanted or Kinain to do for them)?<br /> <br /> I think there is probably some kind of threshold of menace where Fae would go, &quot;Yeah, I normally may not want to involve the local pack of Stag, but I'm glad they are here to deal with this.&quot; It might be because they are hairy murder machines. Or that the masquerade as normal humans, but still tough enough to handle some trouble. Or that they have other supernatural abilities like Gifts that are useful and more prone to work than Fae Arts.<br /> <br /> My assumption is that these threats are usually not Fae in nature, meaning things intrinisic to the Changeling sourcebooks. But other likely supernatural crossover elements, or perhaps more rare menaces mentioned in the Changeling books.<br /> <br /> People might mention the tie between Fomori and Fomorians. However, I am not aware of any specific connections of a fomori type and the Fomorians. I have certain kinds created in my head that I can use, but nothing I know of in canon. So if you go down that route, please provide specifics - either of published foes, or of your own design. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T22:04:57-07:00","id":1403336,"title":"","content":"Remember this the Most Potent Fae could seriously have their greatest magics unwoven by a bitter Librarian who doesn't believe in Fairies, an Autumn Person, such an Enemy could maybe be handled by an Enchanted or Kinain, but if they are say a rich politician or a Mafia Don who is also an Autumn Person then you might want to tap some supernatural assistance.<br /> <br /> And also while Changelings probably Outnumber Garou by a good number a lot of concentrated portable firepower in condensed in a single Garou or a pack. So say during the Accordance War the Local Sidhe war Party is only say 3 Sidhe Knights and 5 Commoner Squires against the entrenched forces of the 30 strong Commoner Militia. They will lose even if you add five more Sidhe Probably unless they are really potent, but a pack of 5 Garou can be a very specific type of help that the local Commoner Militia isn't prepared for. Trolls are strong, but without Dragon's Ire Garou are naturally even stronger.<br /> <br /> Its similar with Garou asking for Fae help with. Fae Arts are naturally very potent and even young Fae might have mastered a specific Art while a Garou have more a grab back of tricks and they need heavy veteran status to unlock their mightiest Gifts. Not to mention the flexibility of Arts can be things like Buffing an already buff pack of Garou.<br /> <br /> One thing I wish was handled was the fact that Sidhe steal bodies and souls, it really feels that a Garou/Sidhe Crusade should have happened at some point.<br /> <br /> And also I just found out reading Shining Host, First Edition had it that Garou were not hampered by the mists, which make sense I don't know why they would not believe in faeries when they already are half spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T07:22:11-07:00","id":1403387,"title":"","content":"Another thing I would note is when the Sidhe Returned they brought with them awareness of Ancient Pacts with the Fianna(especially the Fiona), and Gwydion had similar ones with the Silver Fangs. So early on only a few of the Fianna Galliards would know of specific stories about Pacts, but when the Sidhe start mentioning them I would have Stags Umbrood and Ancestor spirits react very seriously as they could have actually witnessed the original covenants and oaths. Beings like Caern Totems could have even overseen or sanctified them millenia ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T18:56:44-07:00","id":1403455,"title":"","content":"Going along with what Eldagusto has said above, changelings who are able to would desperately like to have the assistance of the Garou with threats of the Autumn World.<br /> <br /> Changeling Cantrips are powerful and both Kinain and the Enchanted are wily opponents, the simple fact is that changelings are losing a slow and dreadful war of attrition against Winter and that even the Kinain and Enchanted can only do so much against the champions of the Autumn World. A Sidhe Knight and a Troll Hero can do great things, but no matter how strong they are and what they can, Autumn will inevitably wear them down into nothing.<br /> <br /> As far as supernatural menaces, Autumn People and Dauntain are obvious but they are still within the paradigm of The Dreaming. Now there are many, many potential supernatural menaces that could face them but I can think of three which would particularly incline the dreamers to ask for garou intervention. Fae Hunters are fairly rare and even then most Changelings are pretty adept at handling foes that don't drown them with Banality and/or Nightmare.<br /> <br /> That being said, what about those threats? Those threats are primarily three imo: Vampires, Ghosts, Demons. All suitably sinister, even if in different ways. That is going to be the concerning element for Changelings of the Dreaming. The Banality and Nightmare these forces bring. <br /> <br /> Young vampires may produce a dark sort of glamour but bloody dreams rapidly become Nightmares and vampires become increasing Banal as they age. All ghosts carry the dread menace of Nightmare and Banality: Nightmare for the dread horrors of the grave and Banality from the horrible reminder of life's ultimate and inevitable end. The Slaugh squeeze as much glamour from death as they can but even for them it's a dangerous abyss to stare into. Demons are naturally rampantly Nightmarish and whether they are Banes or Fallen or whatever else, any denizen of the Dreaming could see Nightmare miasma wherever demons tread.<br /> <br /> Changelings of the Dreaming have to be careful around mundane violence already, as human death is for keeps and thus banal; but these entities are not only dangerous physically but threaten to taint the Dreaming Glamour that these denizens shepherd.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the majority of these beings also reek of the Wyrm and any self-respecting Gaian Garou is unlikely to hesitate to rid the world of such spiritual filth. Perfect synergy.<br /> <br /> There's definitely more ground to cover here but what I will say is that generally, most changelings know they need to be self-sufficient. They band together and fend for themselves, a legacy of the Interregnum. Even the Arcadians who haven't learned such harsh lessons have pride and noble obligation to consider.<br /> <br /> When changelings desperately need help, it is most likely because they desperately need help (even if their reasons may seem frivolous to outsiders and even a few other changelings). Threats to the very essence of who they are almost certainly top that list. Jerry the Redcap will be back in a few days if run through by a Shide Knight and be back in a generation or so if hit by a bus.<br /> <br /> But if Jerry's spirit is perverted and corrupted? If his mien is flayed or if it's violated or if he's cut down with cold iron?<br /> <br /> His dream is over, forever. Winter draws near.<br /> <br /> These threats are when the changelings need the garou most and are in turn probably the most likely to get it, as anything that understands the nature of The Dreaming knows that should the changelings vanish, all glamour and dream is likely to follow soon after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T15:51:26-07:00","id":1403585,"title":"","content":"Now I am thinking of creating a Typhoid Dauntain who is a Changeling who became blood bonded to a vampire (I have several concepts in mind). However, I need a better understanding of how Dauntain is a threat - mechanically - to Changelings. I am not well versed on Changeling mechanics. But I think I need to read a lot more about Banality, and how a character with Banality creates problems for Changeling - both intentionally and unintentionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T21:34:38-07:00","id":1403617,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think they are still pretty unclear about Dauntain. They seem all over the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T22:49:45-07:00","id":1403624,"title":"","content":"Yeah, more could be done to explain what is and is not a Dauntain.<br /> <br /> I generally go with though, any changeling whose mien is perverted, tainted, or damaged by forces of Banality or some other X Factor; and the changeling survives the experience.<br /> <br /> For instance I can definitely see feeding vampire blood to a changeling producing a dauntain. While I'd also say that most changeling miens probably slide into dormancy or undo themselves for survival, I could definitely see 9/10 changelings or those that are forced to live on past a single life time to erupt into a Dauntain and most likely become just as big a problem for the vampire as changelings.<br /> <br /> (I'm also now imagining a Vampire Cautionary Tale about the dangers of ghouling artistic souls who may one day decide to immortalized their love in flame)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T11:44:24-07:00","id":1403694,"title":"","content":"After reading the second edition corebook again and a friend's copy of the Autumn People, it doesn't seem like Dauntain have real mechanical differences. Some Dauntain can make use of Stigmas, but it isn't necessary. Depends on the character concept. They have Banality, but unless it gets to 8 or above, the other Changeling shouldn't react to it. So it's about their Banality being used as a defense against certain Cantrips, and the Dauntain being willing to do things other Changelings won't do because they don't mind destroying the Dreaming and Glamour. (If I understand correctly.)<br /> <br /> So on one hand, it doesn't give me much mechanically to go by. On the other, I can concentrate on the core concept and not be distracted by fiddly bits of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T16:36:35-07:00","id":1403726,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Dauntain are somewhat messy but that goes along with CtD being a game product of the 90s and early 2000s that never got quite the amount of care and attention the Big Three Gamelines did.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Dauntain's strength as antagonists is their ability to harness elements of their twisted chimerical nature alongside forces of Banality to combat the Dreaming. A Dauntain will happily salt and raze the Dreaming around them, regardless of whether it's of the Dream or Nightmare.<br /> <br /> It suffers from a lack of helpful mechanics in some ways but on the other hand it does provide for freedom with development and creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T19:06:51-07:00","id":1404153,"title":"","content":"The original concept of the Dauntain as fairy hunters doesn't map well to the section about Dauntain in the Autumn People sourcebook. Most of them are characters who remain Fae, but simply use Banality to their advantage. Not what was explained to us in the corebook. But they have great variety in the Dauntain types which really helped me brainstorm some ideas.<br /> <br /> I think if I was going to the fairy hunter Dauntain type mentioned in the corebook, I think I'd actually go with something similar to the PC role in Changeling: the Lost. Once the Changeling has rejected their fae mien, and their mortal persona reasserts themselves, they consider themselves to have been &quot;stolen&quot; by the Fae, and only recently managed to return. As a result, they have certain knowledge about the Fae and talents developed during their time of imprisonment/exile in fairyland, and now seek to save their fellow humans who have also been &quot;taken&quot; by the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T23:01:22-07:00","id":1404181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1404153#post1404153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original concept of the Dauntain as fairy hunters doesn't map well to the section about Dauntain in the Autumn People sourcebook. Most of them are characters who remain Fae, but simply use Banality to their advantage. Not what was explained to us in the corebook. But they have great variety in the Dauntain types which really helped me brainstorm some ideas.<br /> <br /> I think if I was going to the fairy hunter Dauntain type mentioned in the corebook, I think I'd actually go with something similar to the PC role in Changeling: the Lost. Once the Changeling has rejected their fae mien, and their mortal persona reasserts themselves, they consider themselves to have been &quot;stolen&quot; by the Fae, and only recently managed to return. As a result, they have certain knowledge about the Fae and talents developed during their time of imprisonment/exile in fairyland, and now seek to save their fellow humans who have also been &quot;taken&quot; by the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that. Yeah I wish they followed this logic, and we could get Dauntain that aren't just Autumn People but Fae. Like the Black Magician Dauntains using Banality as an Arcane concept is intriguing.<br /> <br /> But right now Thallain are infinitely more interesting as antagonists for me because I understand them more and they really make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T23:45:49-07:00","id":1404187,"title":"","content":"It's kind of weird but in a way I almost feel like the Dauntain are more similar in motivation to groups like the Nephandi and Specters then the Thallain are.<br /> <br /> The Thallain are changelings of Nightmare who feed on dark dreams, emotions, and fear. Yet aside from some of the more radical Elder Dark, they don't want to destroy the world - just human civilization and the capacity to Dream instead of dwelling in eternal Nightmare and darkness.<br /> <br /> A fine line to be sure but technically not the nihilistic destructors that antagonize some other gamelines.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Dauntain may not want to plunge all of reality into Nothing's sphincter, they do want to get rid of The Dream or at the very least cut themselves off from it to bring and end to their pain.<br /> <br /> That's why I compare the Dauntain to Specters and Nephandi; they're in pain and surrounded by misery and so they decide that the only reasonable course of reaction is to destroy reality and thus liberate all life from the pains of existence.<br /> <br /> Again most Dauntain probably wouldn't go so far as to destroy the whole world but if they could figure out how to turn the lights out on The Dream for good? I could see them attempting it and even if life survived the process, most people would probably agree it wouldn't exactly be a life worth living.<br /> <br /> Anyway though, that's just my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T00:11:25-07:00","id":1404193,"title":"","content":"Yeah Thallain at least are part of the natural cycle and ecosystem of the Dreaming. Fears and Nightmares balance out Hopes and Dreams in the equation of the Universes Glamour. Without Apocalyptic factors such as Fomorian awakening and treasonous Houses of the Kithain, Thallain are just the Fae that inspire fear in and misery in mortals. Dauntain are broken and have twisted sometimes inverted souls, and that is the province of Nephandi and Specters. Dauntain just don't have dark masters. It could be interesting if they gave Dark Master options for some like Black Magicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T00:37:50-07:00","id":1404196,"title":"","content":"I now have three general Dauntain concepts I could use in my game, so this discussion has been very useful to me.<br /> <br /> The first, as mentioned above, is a Typhoid Dauntain which is a Changeling being blood bonded to a vampire, and as a result of that has succumbed to the power of Banality. This is merely a result of the Changeling's enslavement to his regnant as a property of the blood. He no longer serves the Dreaming, but his master. I have two possible concepts for this. Not sure which one is best, so let me know what you think. The first is that the vampire regnant is an elder Malkavian who recognized the Changeling (likely a Sluagh) for what she is, and was able to blood bond her. This Changeling is now the Malkavian's spy among the Dreaming, and reports back to her. While it is possible for the Malkavian to become some sort of threat to other Changelings, for the most part this is merely curiosity and some hope that in the future, this knowledge may be useful in her intrigues among other Kindred. So the Sluagh is like a secret Dauntain, but could potentially be caught purposefully gaining Banality in order to power Cantrips as well as her disappearances (when she is with her mistress) or odd behavior. The second concept is that a Toreador unknowingly encountered a Changeling at some fancy art power, and was so fascinated she entranced him and later blood bonded. It was quite late when he discovered the mortal he bonded was in fact one of the fae (likely a pooka). That Dauntain drops out of Changeling society and now stays in his haven as a &quot;pet&quot;, with the pooka's form possibly being some kind of predator cat or other dangerous animal.<br /> <br /> The second type of Dauntain is the Cursed Dauntain, a Changeling who took the Oath of Undoing to destroy a hated foe, and now wields terrible power to slay his enemies. For this, I'll be introducing the character as a fae knight early on, befriending the Garou pack should they spend any long time in the Dreaming. But at some point, disaster happens. I am using the D&amp;D stories of Count Strahd and Lord Soth (both had the same creators interestingly enough) as inspirations - noble figures whose passions would destroy them. Trying to develop something that could make the PCs very sympathetic to the villain even when they know they have to destroy him to protect the Dreaming, especially since he was/is their friend.<br /> <br /> The last type is the Dauntain type I just described - a fairy hunter. He went through his Chrysalis a while ago, but recently went through trouble and rejected his fae mien. He now remembers being &quot;stolen&quot; by fairies, but recently &quot;escaped&quot; the fairy realm. He now plans on destroying other fairies (Changelings in general) using the lore he's learned during his &quot;imprisonment&quot; in order to rescue the other people stolen by them. One PC has something in his background that I can use to make this an old friend or family member whose been lost. So it should lead to some great RP when he realizes this friend is now hunting fairies and this directly acting against his totem ban.<br /> <br /> I actually have even more concepts now, but I can only use so many Dauntain concepts before it gets old. I think these three are different enough, and use very different hooks, that I can use them as long as I spread them out and include other the other encounter concepts we've talked about in this thread. And if the PCs actually don't interact that much with the Dreaming, I can pare it down to the best concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T00:47:34-07:00","id":1404197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1404193#post1404193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dauntain just don't have dark masters. It could be interesting if they gave Dark Master options for some like Black Magicians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I definitely think Black Magicians could use a lot more development. We could use all sorts of alternative cantrips or rituals that are available to a Black Magician. Instead, STs need to develop a lot of that ourselves. One possibility is that if being blood bonded is enough to &quot;infect/taint&quot; a Changeling with Banality, then perhaps a Black Magician could make use of such tainted Tass/Banality to do things like vampire Thaumaturgy (either Paths or Rituals, or both), or other inherent banal (yet magical?) things for Infernalist magic. Or just other kind of magic in general.<br /> <br /> But I think all the various Dauntain Dooms could use extensive development. Each needs its own unique flavor to get best use of them. Just saying they use Banality instead of Glamour to fuel Cantrips doesn't do justice to each concept. Such brainstorming could be its own thread on this forum. I think the small page count for each Doom was really evocative and imaginative. Before I read The Autumn People, I didn't think Dauntains could be so extensive. But page count was so short, it really didn't do justice to them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T01:32:38-07:00","id":1404201,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think the Black Magicians should be the types who broke their soul, but got to cheat the system and do things Fae normally can't do.<br /> <br /> What was that Doom with the Dauntain that sloughed off their offal and it could infect others? It was insane, it didn't really give us any rules but said they were a contagious Dauntain?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T12:49:32-07:00","id":1404285,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what &quot;sloughed off their offal&quot; means. I don't think any Dauntain infects others. But Nihilists have an aura that sucks Glamour from others (probably by having the Stigma of Erasure). That sounds most like what you mean. Typhoids are &quot;infected&quot; by someone else's Banality, but despite their name don't seem to spread it to other fae. But if you wanted to make them do so, I guess you could figure out the right concept and give them a Stigma of Conversion (which transforms Glamour into Banality).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T13:12:53-07:00","id":1404291,"title":"","content":"Those Dauntain concepts look cool to me!<br /> <br /> I also agree that there is plenty of ripe ground to further flesh out the Dauntain as a metaphysically active faction. With their potential to operate as the agents of Banality, I can't help but be drawn to how nicely they could form a sort of trinitary relationship with Changelings of the Dreaming and Nightmare.<br /> <br /> Although I also like imagining a neat little trinity of kithain, thallain, and inanimae to represent the Dreaming, Nightmare, and Natural Dreams, so maybe I just like trinities or the Dauntain could serve as a counter balance or the 'Autumn or Winter' of a four phase system.<br /> <br /> I dunno, that's just a lot of random musings really. I also think that maybe coming up with some term to distinguish the 'positive' or 'human' dreams of the kithain from The Dreaming and Dream in general might be useful to this discourse.<br /> <br /> Anyway though, I definitely think that the Dauntain could be more metaphysically fleshed out and in reminded of a recent ST Vault product that fleshed out the Elder Dark when thinking about it, but I can't recall the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T17:11:26-07:00","id":1404320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1404291#post1404291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, that's just a lot of random musings really. I also think that maybe coming up with some term to distinguish the 'positive' or 'human' dreams of the kithain from The Dreaming and Dream in general might be useful to this discourse.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use small &quot;d&quot; dream instead of Dream, I think we could follow it. If you are talking about a dream that is somehow &quot;real&quot; in the sense it can be interacted with, I would just use Chimare from Werewolf. If you really need a separate term that refers to ordinary dreams, maybe something like Phantasma or Sleepdream.<br /> <br /> Usually when the Changeling game talks about &quot;dreams&quot;, it doesn't necessarily mean actual sleeping dreams. But people's hopes, yearnings, and aspirations, or their imagination. So it can be tricky if you want to talk about only one aspect of that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T03:41:34-07:00","id":1404376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1404285#post1404285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what &quot;sloughed off their offal&quot; means. I don't think any Dauntain infects others. But Nihilists have an aura that sucks Glamour from others (probably by having the Stigma of Erasure). That sounds most like what you mean. Typhoids are &quot;infected&quot; by someone else's Banality, but despite their name don't seem to spread it to other fae. But if you wanted to make them do so, I guess you could figure out the right concept and give them a Stigma of Conversion (which transforms Glamour into Banality).</div> </div> </div> </div>page 359 of the C20 book the Brand of the Cadaver, I miss remembered they don't infect others with becoming Dauntain. They do shed essence into a gross dross that spreads a plague where everyone starts shedding essence into contagious gross stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T10:06:38-07:00","id":1404423,"title":"","content":"Wait considering the Stags ban could a Thallain be the one asking for aid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T11:15:10-07:00","id":1404436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1404376#post1404376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">page 359 of the C20 book the Brand of the Cadaver, I miss remembered they don't infect others with becoming Dauntain. They do shed essence into a gross dross that spreads a plague where everyone starts shedding essence into contagious gross stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have C20. I only have some second edition products and those I can borrow from friends.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T11:33:57-07:00","id":1404437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1384313-garou-packs-of-stag-among-the-fae?p=1404423#post1404423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait considering the Stags ban could a Thallain be the one asking for aid?</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially. But in most cases it would likely be foolish to do so unless it is something other fae could also get behind.<br /> <br /> We discussed this earlier in talking about the more treacherous fae asking for help, and what kind of things can be asked. My conclusion is that any fae who asks for help from Garou should be careful. Packs of Stag have an overly broad power to determine for themselves how they can help, so there is limited opportunity for any fae to &quot;control&quot; or manipulate these Garou packs through their oath. The Garou answer to Stag, not any individual Changeling. And packs of Stag will have their pack totem with them to ask for guidance. The Ban shouldn't make Garou help devious fae in their own personal goals, but a broad responsibility to protect the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> In other words, I don't think the Ban should ever place the Garou in a position where Fae think they're the ones who can call the shots (though as ST, I think subtle manipulation is OK) because the Ban puts them in charge (it doesn't). Garou packs of Stag are an independent war band wandering fairy-land. They're likely to come to some kind of agreement with the authority figures of fairy-land, but they don't have any oaths to those kings, dukes, counts, etc. much less to individual fae as a result of the Ban. They just need to make Stag happy.<br /> <br /> And those fae who could be considered potential enemies of the Garou are merely bringing themselves to their attention. Nothing would prevent the Garou from &quot;aiding&quot; the Thallain, and then attacking them if they thought that best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T06:45:34-07:00","id":1404582,"title":"","content":"Wait yeah I wonder about a pack of Werewolves in the dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}